#=GF RM 8045882
#=GF RT Interaction between the acceptor end of tRNA and the T box stimulates
#=GF RT antitermination in the Bacillus subtilis tyrS gene: a new role for the
#=GF RT discriminator base.
#=GF RA Grundy FJ, Rollins SM, Henkin TM
#=GF RL J Bacteriol 1994;176:4518-4526.
#=GF RN [2]
#=GF RM 10943892
#=GF RT tRNA determinants for transcription antitermination of the Bacillus
#=GF RT subtilis tyrS gene.
#=GF RA Grundy FJ, Collins JA, Rollins SM, Henkin TM
#=GF RL RNA 2000;6:1131-1141.
#=GF RN [3]
#=GF RM 11497434
#=GF RT The GA motif: an RNA element common to bacterial antitermination systems,
#=GF RT rRNA, and eukaryotic RNAs.
#=GF RA Winkler WC, Grundy FJ, Murphy BA, Henkin TM
#=GF RL RNA 2001;7:1165-1172.
#=GF RN [4]
#=GF RM 12547201
#=GF RT Solution structure of the Bacillus subtilis T-box antiterminator RNA:
#=GF RT seven nucleotide bulge characterized by stacking and flexibility.
#=GF RA Gerdeman MS, Henkin TM, Hines JV
#=GF RL J Mol Biol 2003;326:189-201.
#=GF CC Uncharged tRNA acts as the effector for transcription antitermination of
#=GF CC genes in the T-box leader family [1-3]. T-boxes are found upstream of many
#=GF CC aminoacyl-tRNA synthetase genes and some amino acid biosynthetic genes
#=GF CC usually in Gram-positive bacteria. The anticodon of a specific tRNA base
#=GF CC pairs to a specifier sequence within the T-box motif, and the NCCA
#=GF CC acceptor tail of the tRNA base pairs to a conserved bulge in the T-box
#=GF CC antiterminator hairpin [4].
#=GF WK T-box_leader
#=GF SQ 48

